WEBVTT

00:59:27.538 --> 00:59:32.371
No exaggeration. I think I have back to
back had the two jobs that are at least

00:59:32.371 --> 00:59:34.454
the most interesting to me
in all of Silicon Valley.

00:59:34.663 --> 00:59:38.996
I, I was I went to college to
study computer science.

00:59:38.996 --> 00:59:41.038
I was a major computer nerd growing up.

00:59:41.246 --> 00:59:43.829
I knew like a little bit about startups,
but not very much.

00:59:44.121 --> 00:59:47.454
I started working on this project the
same year I started working on that.

00:59:47.454 --> 00:59:51.788
This thing called Y Combinator started
and funded me and my co-founders.

00:59:52.163 --> 00:59:54.996
And we dropped out of school
and did this company,

00:59:55.746 --> 00:59:59.704
which I ran for like seven years. And
then after that I got acquired.

00:59:59.954 --> 01:00:01.829
I had stayed close to my
comment the whole time.